\DOC STRIP_EXISTS_ASSUM_TAC

\TYPE {STRIP_EXISTS_ASSUM_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Strips an existentially quantified, conjunctive assumption from the goal,
replacing it by its conjuncts as separate assumptions with the existential
variables freed.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. It searches the assumption list for an assumption of the
form {?x1 ... xn. u1 /\ ... /\ uk} (with n at least one and k at least two),
deletes it, and appends the conjuncts as individual assumptions in which
{x1 ... xn} now occur free; the conclusion is unchanged.
{
   A, (?x1 ... xn. u1 /\ ... /\ uk) ?- t
   ======================================  STRIP_EXISTS_ASSUM_TAC
   A, u1, ..., uk ?- t
}

\FAILURE
Fails (a "tryfind" failure, i.e. no candidate assumption was suitable) on goals
whose assumption lists contain no assumption of the required existentially
quantified form, including goals where all assumptions are plain equations,
non-overlap conditions, or universally quantified statements.

\COMMENTS
In the observed traces, only a single existential assumption is processed per
application, the conclusion is never touched, and the goals are all of the same
assembly-reasoning shape.

\ENDDOC
